    "description": "New Leaf Energy develops utility-scale, commercial, and community solar and storage projects for utilities, corporate offtakers, and community energy programs in the United States. The company operates as a development platform that originates sites, secures permits and interconnection, advances offtake arrangements, and manages projects through financing and construction handoff. Its model is development-led and contracted rather than merchant, with value tied to a pipeline of permitted and construction-ready projects across multiple power markets. ECP and company materials describe a development portfolio of approximately 15 gigawatts of solar and 7 gigawatts of storage, which provides a large national scale indicator for the platform. The business was formed in July 2022 through the spin-off of Borrego's development business backed by ECP, and it now operates as a standalone renewables developer under that ownership.",
